  "body": "PR985 gives a conservative O(r\u00b3 W_total) allowance for sequential factor lookup. This research audit proves that its unchanged balanced word admits quadratic factor-tape travel under an explicit contiguous, fixed-width layout.\n\nFor every n \u2265 1 and both call directions, the closed index travel is less than 2N, where N = 3qn \u2212 2q\u00b2 and q = 2^floor(log2 n). A reader that copies every B-bit descriptor and restores its head uses fewer than 4NB descriptor-head moves and exactly NB payload reads. The complete lookup bound is P_layout + P_parse + O(G + N(B + log\u00b2(nB+2))); setup, parsing, common parameters, preflight, copies, and amortized control are explicit. The proof also gives the exact quadratic variation on powers of two.\n\nThis refines a safe access allowance, not a false predecessor theorem. Preparation, numerical precision, arithmetic, mutable-array routing, recursive children, and physical/compiler obligations remain paid separately. It does not certify PR1054's complete invoice, improve the selected \u03ba, or claim a measured runtime gain.\n\n## Verification\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -O -B research/balanced-descriptor-travel/test_package.py\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_DESCRIPTOR_PACKAGE` with a nested `PASS_BALANCED_DESCRIPTOR_TRAVEL` receipt.\n\n- 150,126 actual lookups from the byte-exact PR985 dispatcher across 78 signed cases; two further cases vary array geometry.\n- A separate compressed word algebra checks 4,241 counts. Literal bit-head and countdown models check 102 tape cases and 1,025 counter cases.\n- Nine mathematical/tape controls and five package faults reject. The full audit passes from a read-only relocated copy.\n- All five vendor files match their pinned Git blobs. Selected-record integrity and all 25 selected-result tests pass. CPython 3.15.0, standard library only.\n\nThe all-size claim rests on the written induction and paid reader construction. The main dispatcher fixtures use length-one arrays and zero coefficients to exercise the fixed dispatch structure; these are not numerical precision tests. Independent checking means separate implementations/models, not independent human review. Full repository/cold supplier replay, hosted CI, and formal verification of the multiplication theorem are not claimed.\n\n## Scope and attribution\n\nOnly `research/balanced-descriptor-travel/` is added. The publication base is `1b59b624d21924f8e3537cdc1ac52d3be6eda2fe`; the experiment source is PR985 `da1cdf8ed4ac9b1b8378dfec73f77ff4e81a4f70`. The local seed-65 claim records continuation, finite domains, inspected heads, current discussion review and overlap checks through PR1206. PR1054, PR1085, PR1135, and discussion1202 concern different precision, magnitude, or representation questions.\n\nCredit Ali Romman for PR985, Chafik Boukhalfa for PR628's balanced commutator and preparation lineage, and 0xkilgore for PR663's leaf count. Retained licenses and predecessor notices are unchanged. Prepared by Charles Bethin with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in derivation, implementation, verification, and writing. No literature-priority claim or external human review.\n",
